&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on the Cloud Infrastructure team, you&#39;ll build automation and evolve the foundational systems that support Gusto&#39;s products. This is a code-driven infrastructure role, well suited to someone with a DevOps, SRE, or platform engineering background who enjoys solving problems that help other engineers work more effectively. You&#39;ll help set the architecture, Infrastructure-as-Code patterns, and operational standards that every Gusto engineer builds on, with real autonomy over how it gets done. Key opportunities include migrating production applications into a modern AWS multi-account architecture, strengthening disaster recovery and compliance, and improving the speed and reliability of our infrastructure tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto&#39;s Cloud Infrastructure team builds and operates the AWS foundations that the rest of our engineering organization depends on. We manage infrastructure as code with Terraform/OpenTofu and run Spacelift, the platform hundreds of engineers use daily to deploy infrastructure changes. This experienced team partners with networking, compute, platform, and application teams to make Gusto&#39;s cloud infrastructure more reliable, resilient, and easier to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what you’ll do day-to-day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain AWS infrastructure using Terraform/OpenTofu, with changes managed through code rather than manual configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the speed, reliability, and usability of Spacelift workflows used by engineering teams across Gusto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with application and infrastructure teams to migrate production services into a modern AWS multi-account architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen disaster recovery and compliance readiness by implementing and testing infrastructure resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refactor infrastructure code into modular, reusable components that simplify maintenance and future development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support engineering teams with cloud infrastructure needs, troubleshooting, and vendor integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI-assisted tools to accelerate infrastructure development, improve troubleshooting, and identify automation opportunities while maintaining a high bar for security, correctness, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation focused on internal engineering support, turning recurring issues into automation and lasting improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on experience in infrastructure, platform, or site reliability engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, production-level AWS expertise across compute, networking, identity, and security primitives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated mastery of Infrastructure as Code &lt;em&gt;(Terraform/OpenTofu strongly preferred; Crossplane, CloudFormation, or similar)&lt;/em&gt; including module design, state management, and scalable patterns for large teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-account AWS governance — AWS Organizations, OU design, SCPs/RCPs, and federated identity via IAM Identity Center or equivalent SSO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with a managed IaC orchestration platform &lt;em&gt;(Spacelift, Terraform Cloud, etc.)&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating production infrastructure for a customer-facing SaaS platform, including observability &lt;em&gt;(monitoring, logging, alerting)&lt;/em&gt; and participating in incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving multi-quarter infrastructure initiatives to completion with minimal direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating Terraform/OpenTofu at large scale — managing thousands of workspaces or state files, module registries and versioning strategy, drift detection and remediation, and policy-as-code enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in compliance-regulated environments (SOC 2, PCI, NIST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid cloud networking foundations: VPC design, IP address management, DNS, egress control, and centralized traffic inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
