&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for seasoned full-stack software engineers to join Gusto’s PEO Benefits team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gusto is standing up a Professional Employer Organization (PEO) — one of the biggest new bets in the company — and Benefits is the anchor of the offering. At the core is a national Master Health Plan that can unlock ~20–25% lower healthcare costs for small businesses through pooled purchasing power, something most PEOs can&#39;t pull off in year one. You&#39;d be joining the engineering team building the systems that make that real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is rare greenfield scope inside a company with real scale and real customers. You get to make foundational architectural decisions, not maintain someone else&#39;s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer, you&#39;ll operate across the full product lifecycle: shaping features from early spec and design through to launch and long-term iteration. That means writing clean frontend code, designing and building reliable backend APIs, influencing product direction, and taking ownership of what happens after a feature ships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re drawn to work that combines technical craft with real-world impact — helping power the livelihoods of millions using Gusto products — join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what you’ll do day-to-day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, build, and test&lt;/strong&gt; the Gusto PEO Benefits experience - the benefits shopping and plan-recommendation flows, carrier integrations, MCP tools, agents that automate operational and customer support processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers to help solve some of the hardest technical problems out there in very complex domains and at a large scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale one of the largest Ruby/Rails and Javascript/React applications in the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our Product Management, Data, Design, and Platform Engineering teams to understand customer pain points, come up with solutions, and then &lt;strong&gt;prototype, iterate, and launch daily&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build products that our &lt;strong&gt;customers genuinely love&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful applicants typically have 8+ years of software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PEO Expertise (Preferred):&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of experience with PEO, with direct experience building PEO flows in a high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning multi-quarter projects that solve complex engineering problems and make measurable customer impact at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving large, cross-functional projects end-to-end through ambiguity — scoping, sequencing, and unblocking without needing the problem pre-broken-down; aligning multiple stakeholders and working with multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience leveraging AI tools or systems to accelerate development, improve testing, and deliver new product capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity and experimentation with emerging AI frameworks&lt;/strong&gt;, applying and sharing best practices to evaluate and scale AI use safely across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to mentor engineers to maximize their performance and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Others:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in, or interest working in, Ruby on Rails&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appreciation for a collaborative, test-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build well-structured, maintainable, well-documented code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively communicate across engineering teams and with business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
