&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a staff software engineer to join Tax Accounts — the team whose job is to make the complexity of dealing with hundreds of tax agencies disappear. We&#39;re the steward of every Gusto customer&#39;s employer and employee tax account data: the registrations, authorizations, rates, and setup that let us withhold, pay, and file correctly on their behalf. Get it right and businesses stay compliant without thinking about it; get it wrong and it costs them real money and trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on Tax Accounts, you&#39;ll operate across the full product lifecycle: clean frontend code, reliable backend APIs and data models against a genuinely complex compliance domain, and the automation that keeps hundreds of thousands of accounts in sync with the agencies behind them. If you want technical craft with far-reaching impact in our modern economy helping power the livelihoods of millions of small business employees — join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what you’ll do day-to-day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and test the systems behind employer and employee tax accounts: agency registrations, power-of-attorney / third-party authorizations, tax notices, agency filings, and state/federal/employee tax setup across jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation that requests and maintains access with tax agencies on the customer&#39;s behalf — the bots, data exchanges, and agency-event pipelines that keep accounts, rates, and deposit schedules accurate and prevent failed filings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model complex, jurisdiction-specific compliance rules into maintainable systems, and own reliability, performance, and correctness in a domain where accuracy is non-negotiable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Design, Tax Operations, and PEO teams to turn customer and compliance pain into solutions — then prototype, iterate, and launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and help the team solve some of the hardest problems in a very complex domain, at large scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build products that our customers genuinely love&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant software-development experience, typically 8+ years, with demonstrated staff-level technical leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning multi-quarter projects that solve complex engineering problems and make measurable customer impact at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable solutions that eliminate customer pain, and a strong sense of ownership over reliability, performance, and correctness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort designing data models and APIs for a complex, rules-heavy domain (compliance, tax, payments, or similar) where edge cases and correctness matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI tools or systems to accelerate development, improve testing, and deliver new capabilities — plus curiosity and experimentation with emerging AI frameworks, and a habit of sharing best practices to scale AI use safely across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to mentor engineers to maximize their performance and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively across engineering teams and with business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
